  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide Lifesaving Multi Sectoral Assistance to South Sudan Returnees Affected by Sudan Crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) as well as Common Services assistance to vulnerable people in South Sudan fleeing fighting in Sudan. This IOM project establishes and manages reception and transit centres, coordinates humanitarian assistance delivered by partners, supports onward transport assistance, and conducts flow monitoring at points of entry. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 7,200 people in the CCCM sector and 10,615 people in the Common Services sector.</narrative>
  </description>
